    "lawCode": "Amd §36, Munic Home R L",
    "lawSection": "Municipal Home Rule Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:A10172\n\nTITLE  OF  BILL:    An  act  to  amend the municipal home rule law, in\nrelation to charter revision commissions\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF  BILL:  This  bill  clearly  lays  out  the\nprocess  for  a charter revision commission to follow. It requires the\ncommission to hold a hearing or hearings before it begins its work and\nagain after it  presents  preliminary  proposals  to  the  public.  It\nrequires  that  any  proposals  put before The voters be placed on the\nballot as separate proposals to the extent practicable. It prevents  a\ncommission  formed  after  February  15  in  any  given  year to place\nproposals on the ballot in that year.\n\nJUSTIFICATION: This bill sets forth the process of charter revision in\nsuch a way as to provide for  the  public  to  propose  and  react  to\nproposals.  It  provides time for deliberative thinking on the part of\nall parties, both the members of the commission and the public  and  a\nchance to fully educate the voters as to any proposals they might vote\nupon.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY: New bill.\n\nEFFECTIVE  DATE:  January 1, 2010 and provides for any commission that\nis in the process of deliberations not in compliance with this act  is\nterminated.\n\n",
