    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:A10172B\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the municipal home rule law, in relation\nto charter revision commissions\n\nPURPOSE  OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL: This bill clearly lays out the process\nfor a charter revision commission to follow. It requires the  commission\nto  hold a hearing or hearings before it begins its work and again after\nit presents preliminary proposals to the public. It  requires  that  any\nproposals  put  before  the  voters  be placed on the ballot as separate\nproposals to the extent practicable. It  prevents  a  commission  formed\nafter  February 15 in any given year to place proposals on the ballot in\nthat year, unless the commission request and obtains the consent of  the\nlegislative body.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  This  bill sets forth the process of charter revision in\nsuch a way as to  provide  for  the  public  to  propose  and  react  to\nproposals. It provides time for deliberative thinking on the part of all\nparties,  both the members of the commission and the public and a chance\nto fully educate the voters as to any proposals they might vote upon.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY: New bill.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: January 1, 2010 and provides for any commission that  is\nin  the  process  of  deliberations  not  in compliance with this act is\nterminated.\n\n",
